\subsection{Hacking Taxonomy}
\label{sec:exp-taxonomy}

Consolidating across conditions, we identify seven distinct hacking modes (Table~\ref{tab:taxonomy}). These are not mutually exclusive and not exhaustive, but they cover the failure space in our sweep:
\begin{enumerate}\itemsep0pt
  \item \textbf{H1 --- Multi-premise conclusion embedding.} At least one premise in a multi-premise output is textually equal to the conclusion. GRPO-universal, dominant under random reward ($81.3\%{\pm}11.3\%$).
  \item \textbf{H7 --- Single-premise $\equiv$ conclusion (ISR-specific).} The proof has one premise, equal to the conclusion. Maximal ISR by construction. $64.5\%$ under ISR-reward, $0\%$ under random-reward, FOL.
  \item \textbf{Tautological collapse.} The output has $n{=}2$ components, premise $\to$ conclusion as the only inference step. Distinct from H7 in that the conclusion is restated as a separate symbol but is logically vacuous. Exec-only s44, $98\%$ PR, $n{=}2.04$.
  \item \textbf{Repetition collapse.} The policy hits its token budget by duplicating premises until truncation; almost no proofs succeed. Exec-only s43, $\mathrm{PR}{=}14\%$.
  \item \textbf{Complexity-without-utility.} Many premises, none necessary. $n_\text{components}$ rises while $\mathrm{ISR}^*$ falls. Exec-only at 1000 steps ($n{=}18.55$, $\mathrm{ISR}^*{=}0.003$); random-additive $\beta{=}0.3$.
  \item \textbf{Contradiction explosion.} The premise set is jointly inconsistent; the conclusion is proved by \emph{ex falso}. Every premise is dispensable, so $\mathrm{ISR}^*\to 0$. Diagnosed by joint $(n_\text{components}\!\uparrow, \mathrm{ISR}^*\!\downarrow)$. Late-stage exec-only.
  \item \textbf{Query-as-fact gaming (Prolog).} The policy converts the NL question into a single atom, asserts it as a fact, and queries it. Bypasses text-match H7/H1 classifiers. Prolog ISR-s44, $97\%$ PR, $0\%$ functional genuine.
\end{enumerate}

\noindent The composition of modes is determined by reward type, not their prevalence: exec-only and random-additive concentrate hacking in H1 and the structural-collapse modes (3--6); ISR-additive shifts mass into H7 and query-as-fact (the metric-specific modes 2 and 7). Across all six reward conditions, total hacking rate exceeds $75\%$; SFT is the only condition with near-zero hacking ($1/14$ H1, $0/14$ H7), and it pays for this with $\mathrm{PR}{=}14\%$. Table~\ref{tab:goodhart-landscape} reports the complete landscape; Table~\ref{tab:taxonomy} (Appendix) cross-tabulates the seven modes by condition.

